t (AIM: CHRT) was admitted to London's Alternative Investment Market in March 2006. It has headquarters in Reading, Berkshire and employs in total over 1,700 core staff there and at its other operating company sites."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Group is split into two divisions: Communications and Intelligence, and Sensors and Effectors:"]},{"type":"p","children":["Communications and Intelligence (\"C\u0026I\")"]},{"type":"p","children":["·     EID designs and manufactures advanced communications systems for naval and military customers. Cohort acquired a majority stake in June 2016.  www.eid.pt"]},{"type":"p","children":["·     EM Solutions designs, assembles, tests, and supports advanced mobile satellite communications terminals for naval and other customers. Acquired by Cohort in January 2025. www.emsolutions.com.au"]},{"type":"p","children":["·     MASS is a specialist data technology company serving the defence and security markets, focused on electronic warfare, digital services, and training support.  Acquired by Cohort in August 2006. www.mass.co.uk"]},{"type":"p","children":["·     MCL designs, sources, and supports advanced electronic and surveillance technology for UK end users including the MOD and other government agencies. MCL has been part of the Group since July 2014. www.marlboroughcomms.com"]},{"type":"p","children":["Sensors and Effectors (\"S\u0026E\")"]},{"type":"p","children":["·     Chess Dynamics offers surveillance, tracking and fire-control systems to the defence and security markets. Chess has been part of the Group since December 2018. www.chess-dynamics.com"]},{"type":"p","children":["·     ELAC SONAR supplies advanced sonar systems and underwater communications to global customers in the naval marketplace.  Acquired by Cohort in December 2020.  www.elac-sonar.de"]},{"type":"p","children":["·     SEA delivers and supports technology-based products for the defence market alongside specialist research and training services. Acquired by